        "comments": "The assembly bColMon1.hap2.1 is based on 77x PacBio data and Arima2 Hi-C data generated by the Darwin Tree of Life Project\n(https://www.darwintreeoflife.org/). The assembly process included the following sequence of steps: initial PacBio assembly generation with Hifiasm in Hi-C integrated assembly mode, and Hi-C based scaffolding with YaHS. The mitochondrial genome was assembled using MitoHiFi. Finally, each haplotype assembly was analysed and manually improved using TreeVal. Chromosome-scale scaffolds confirmed by the Hi-C data have been named in order of size. The exact order and orientation of the contigs on chromosome 1 (55.5 - 59 Mbp), chromosome 8 (12 - 14 Mbp) are unknown. The microchromosomes were identified through second-shot curation of scaffolds smaller than 20 Mbp, combined with homology-based identification using known microchromosome genes via MicroFinder. Chromosomes Z and W were identified by copy number in the diploid assembly. A large number of centromeric repeats is in the unlocalised sequences.",
